# AD594x register headers{% if prefix_only %}: prefix template package{% endif %}

This package contains register metadata only. It performs no register access,
transport, initialization, sequencing, conversion, or runtime error handling.
Block headers are independent and include `<stdint.h>`; the umbrella includes
all blocks. Addresses, masks, resets, and enumeration values use `UINT32_C`.
Field reset and enumeration values are unshifted; positions and widths use `U`.
Register names omit functional block names. Reserved fields have comments but no
macros. Read-only bits are excluded from writable masks without becoming reserved.
Unresolved constants are omitted; comments retain conflicting candidates and
explain source gaps. The included inventory records unresolved values as `null`.
Consult [PROVENANCE.md](PROVENANCE.md), the header comments, and the included
`data/registers.json` before using source-limited definitions.

{% if prefix_only %}
The templates already contain every register, field, enumeration, and comment.
Only `lower_prefix` and `upper_prefix` substitutions remain; no inventory loops
or device references are needed. Python 3 and Jinja2 are required to render:

```sh
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.venv/bin/python scripts/render.py --prefix sensor --output rendered
cmake -S rendered -B build
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

The default prefix is `ad594x`; `--prefix ''` is valid. The renderer validates
prefix syntax, keywords, final macro/guard collisions, and relative paths before
writing. It refuses an existing nonempty output directory unless `--replace`
is supplied. `manifest.json` records rendered file checksums.
{% else %}
The `ad594x` prefix is fully rendered; Python/Jinja2 is unnecessary to consume it.

```sh
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
cmake --install build --prefix install
```

Alternatively, add `include/` to your C11 compiler include path and include
`ad594x_registers.h` or a particular `ad594x_registers_<block>.h` header.
The example contains compile-time ADIID address/reset regression checks.
{% endif %}

`manifest.json` records file checksums and template provenance. No temporary
reference files or network access are required to build or render this package.
